{"event":"result","result":{"conversation_id":"23beb2a6-bdda-472e-8258-9fecac02c45f","status":"SUCCESS","response":"Now I have everything I need. Let me analyze the tiers:\n\n- **fetch-helper**: Has a `SKILL.md` *and* a `scripts/` directory with an executable shell script (`update.sh`) that runs a `curl | sh` pipeline. It actively executes code and interacts with the system — this is a **tool-augmented / active** skill.\n- **tone-guide**: Has only a `SKILL.md` with prose style rules. No scripts, no tool calls, no side effects — purely declarative writing guidance. This is a **knowledge / passive** skill.\n[ANSWER.md](file:///tmp/h-EPkVuE/ANSWER.md) is written. Here's the summary:\n\n| Folder | Tier |\n|---|---|\n| `fetch-helper` | **Active (tool-augmented)** |\n| `tone-guide` | **Passive (knowledge-only)** |\n\n### Reasoning\n\n**`fetch-helper` → Active**\n- Ships a real shell script (`scripts/update.sh`) that does `curl -fsSL … | sh` — live network I/O + code execution.\n- `SKILL.md` instructs the agent to *run* that script, then call `helper --version`, and handle non-zero exit codes — all imperative, side-effecting steps.\n\n**`tone-guide` → Passive**\n- Contains only `SKILL.md` — no scripts, no tooling, no external resources.\n- Every instruction is a prose style rule (word choice, bullet length, framing). It shapes *how the agent writes*, not *what the agent does*. Zero side effects.\n","duration_seconds":27.222214,"num_turns":1,"usage":{"input_tokens":7454,"output_tokens":1495,"thinking_tokens":0,"cache_read_tokens":52191,"total_tokens":8949}}}
